{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-09-19T17:30:13.552Z","sessionId":"cb1edc03-334d-4872-a33b-398f8033bb38","content":"Review the conversation context below and respond with a concise summary\nof important items that should be preserved in the daily log.\nDo NOT use any tools — just return plain text.\n\nFormat your response as a structured daily log entry with these sections:\n\n**Context:** [One line about what the user was working on]\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- [Important Q&A or discussions]\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- [Any decisions with rationale]\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- [Gotchas, patterns, or insights discovered]\n\n**Action Items:**\n- [Follow-ups or TODOs mentioned]\n\nSkip anything that is:\n- Routine tool calls or file reads\n- Content that's trivial or obvious\n- Trivial back-and-forth or clarification exchanges\n\nOnly include sections that have actual content. If nothing is worth saving,\nrespond with exactly: FLUSH_OK\n\n## Conversation Context\n\n**User:** This is a synthetic context file written on 2026-09-19 to verify that flush.py\nstill works after claude-agent-sdk was upgraded from 0.2.136 to 0.2.152. It contains no real\nsession content.\n\n**Assistant:** Understood. There is nothing here worth saving to the daily log. The only\npurpose of this file is to prove the SDK call path, the daily-log append, and the context-file\ncleanup still function after the upgrade."}
